    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353-a2">

                <pb facs="0522" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg402"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Dawson to
                        General Sanchez.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to the subject of our
                    conversation of this morning, I have the honor to inform your excellency that if
                    it is agreeable to this government the President of the United States will,
                    under a Congressional resolution approved June 22, 1898, issue a proclamation
                    prohibiting the exportation of arms and ammunition from the United States to
                    this Republic.</p>
                <p>All such exportation would therefore become unlawful unless specially authorized
                    by the American Government, and my government would of course promptly give such
                    authority in any cases desired by the Dominican Government.</p>
                <p>I improve, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
